---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Shell
  current="mesh"
  title="Mesh — relay topology · The Grid"
  description="The MeshCore mesh as a topology map: every located node (colored by role) with the relay links reconstructed from each advert's path — the repeater chain it traversed, resolved to mapped nodes. Built from GET /api/v1/events?layer=mesh."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/maplibre-gl.css" />
    <style is:global>
      .mesh-topbar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 18px; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
      #mesh-stats { font-size: 13.5px; }
      #mesh-window { display: inline-flex; gap: 4px; }
      .mesh-win-btn {
        font: inherit; font-size: 12px; padding: 3px 9px; cursor: pointer;
        color: var(--text-2); background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border);
        /* radii-0: the broadsheet has no pills. */
      }
      .mesh-win-btn:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--text-faint); }
      .mesh-win-btn.active { color: var(--text-hi); border-color: var(--accent-cyan, #6aa9c9); background: rgba(106, 169, 201, 0.14); }
      #mesh-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 14px; margin-left: auto; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-2); }
      .mesh-leg { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
      .mesh-dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; border: 1px solid #0b0f12; }
      #mesh-canvas {
        width: 100%; height: 620px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: var(--ink); overflow: hidden;
      }
      /* Popup: an ink surface over the dark basemap, mirroring the map page —
         no radius, no drop shadow, and the .on-ink severity ramp. */
      .maplibregl-popup-content {
        background: var(--ink); color: var(--on-ink-2); border: 1px solid var(--ink-rule);
        font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; padding: 10px 12px; box-shadow: none;
        --sev-EXTREME: #ff5544; --sev-SEVERE: #e0913f; --sev-MODERATE: #d0a24a;
        --sev-MINOR: #4d9c3a; --sev-INFO: #3d8bff;
      }
      .maplibregl-popup-close-button { color: var(--on-ink-muted); font-size: 17px; }
      .map-popup .popup-headline { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: var(--on-ink); margin-bottom: 5px; }
      .map-popup .popup-chips { margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .mesh-roletag { font-weight: 600; }
      .popup-details-dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 2px 12px; margin: 0; }
      .popup-details-dl dt { color: var(--text-fainter); font-size: 11px; }
      .popup-details-dl dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      @media (max-width: 720px) { #mesh-canvas { height: 66vh; } #mesh-legend { margin-left: 0; } }
    </style>
  </Fragment>

  <PageHead kicker="Relay topology" title="Mesh">
    <p class="lead">
      The whole MeshCore mesh as a topology map — every located node from
      <code class="inline">GET /api/v1/events?layer=mesh</code>, colored by role, with the
      <strong>relay links</strong> from
      <code class="inline">GET /api/v1/mesh/links</code>: the server rolls up each advert's relay
      path over time into a durable, weighted edge list. Links <strong>fade by recency</strong>
      (a quiet-but-recent link is dim, not gone) and thicken with traffic; the window control trades
      currency for history, so an intermittent, shaky mesh reads honestly. Coverage is deliberately
      wide (Bay Area → Sierra). <strong class="accent-orange">A sparse map is not an all-clear — a
      node is only drawn once we've heard it advertise a location.</strong>
    </p>
  </PageHead>

  <div class="mesh-topbar">
    <div id="mesh-stats" class="muted">Loading the mesh…</div>
    <div id="mesh-window" aria-label="Time window"></div>
    <div id="mesh-legend"></div>
  </div>

  <div id="mesh-canvas"></div>
  <div id="mesh-errors" class="section-gap"></div>

  <!-- The node roster. The map answers "where is the mesh"; this answers "what
       exactly did we hear, and how long ago" — including nodes whose telemetry
       is partial, which a map dot cannot express. -->
  <div class="section-gap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="left"><h2>Nodes heard</h2></div>
      <span class="cap">node · type · snr / rssi · hops · heard</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose" style="font-size:13.5px;">
      Mesh presence is ambient <code class="inline">INFO</code> state: it is excluded from a place's
      <code class="inline">totalActive</code>, its severity counts, its top events and its area mode —
      a busy mesh does not raise an alert level, and a quiet one does not lower it.
      Telemetry (SNR, RSSI, hop count) is <strong>volatile and deliberately excluded from the content
      hash</strong>, so it never mints a revision; only a node's identity, location or status does.
      <strong class="accent-orange">To ask when a node last spoke, read the event's
      <code class="inline">observedAt</code>, not <code class="inline">telemetry.lastAdvertAt</code></strong>
      — the latter is stamped by the node's own unsynchronized clock. Missing telemetry renders as
      <span class="mono">—</span>, never as <span class="mono">0</span>.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Node</th><th style="width:130px">Type</th>
            <th style="width:140px">SNR / RSSI</th>
            <th class="num" style="width:70px">Hops</th>
            <th style="width:150px">Heard</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="mesh-tbody"><tr><td colspan="5"><span class="loading">Loading nodes…</span></td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline src="/lib/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <script is:inline type="module">
    import { initMeshPage } from '/assets/pages/mesh.js';
    initMeshPage();
  </script>
</Shell>
